  "purpose": "Determine whether llama.cpp's KV cache can be placed on a different backend device than a layer's own model weights, via a minimal, additive llama.cpp patch (kv_dev_override), closing the coupling gap Phase 12A identified (12A precedes this chain and is not an ancestor of it).",
  "literal_verdict": "KV_DEVICE_OVERRIDE_VIABLE",
  "verdict_summary": "A minimal (68 insertions/7 deletions, 6 files) additive llama.cpp patch adding a kv_dev_override callback makes KV cache device placement independently selectable from weight placement. Default behavior is provably byte-identical when unset (verified null/always-null/always-default-callback equivalence). Per-layer placement was cross-validated three independent ways with zero mismatches. Real, KV-attributable external VRAM reduction was measured (12-96 MiB depending on context) and a previously-unrunnable configuration (ctx=200000 on GTX 1650) became runnable with zero weight movement. Correctness (token-identical generation across placement ratios) and orthogonality to KV precision (Q8_0/Q5_1) were both confirmed.",
  "verdict_source": "results/phase12/kv-device-override/summary.json:decision_gate / decision_gate_rationale (literal source fields, not synthesized)",
  "productized": true,
  "product_pr": 21,
  "product_commit": "8287e8c14f1b5af2e9e17fa95e85663e94697d85",
  "productization_note": "The llama.cpp-side patch itself (patches/llama.cpp-membrane-kv-device-override.patch) is byte-for-byte identical between this research branch and product main (verified: diff exit 0) -- the kv_dev_override callback shipped in PR #21 unchanged. The research-side policy code (tools/membrane-kv-device-override/split_policy.c, a minimal fixed-split decider) is NOT byte-identical to the product's planner (tools/membrane-run/kv_residency_policy.c, a full VRAM-budget-based per-layer planner) -- the product planner is a materially more sophisticated, independently-written module that consumes the same kv_dev_override capability this phase proved viable. Do not treat the two C policy files as the same code.",
  "reproducibility": "PARTIALLY_REPRODUCIBLE",
  "hardware": "NVIDIA GTX 1650 (4096 MiB VRAM), Vulkan backend",
  "models": [
    "SmolLM2-135M-Instruct",
    "SmolLM2-360M-Instruct"
  ],
